<title>USA: Rockwell semiconductor earnings lower.</title>
<headline>Rockwell semiconductor earnings lower.</headline>
<dateline>SEAL BEACH, Calif. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rockwell International Corp said Tuesday that fiscal second quarter profits at its semiconductor systems business were down 13 percent from a year earlier due to the transition to new K56flex modem chipsets.</p>
<p>The company said shipments of the new chipsets, which allow modems to communicate twice as fast as previously, are expected to reach one million per month by the end of the fiscal third quarter, which began April 1.</p>
<p>Second quarter revenue growth was paced by its industrial automation unit, where earnings were up 21 percent from last year. Automation sales rose 10 percent, to $1.1 billion.</p>
<p>Avionics and communications earnings were more than double the year-earlier results, it said.</p>
